== notation: symbols used in L04-L06 vs notation.json
notation keys: ['schema', 'about', 'macros', 'symbols']
registered symbols count 8
   T | number of return observations (periods) in a sample
   \Phi, \Phi^{-1} | standard normal CDF and its inverse (quantile function)
   \gamma_3 | skewness of returns, E[(r-\mu)^3]/\sigma^3
   \gamma_4 | kurtosis of returns (not excess), E[(r-\mu)^4]/\sigma^4; 3 under normality
   R^\ast | the return on the SDF in the payoff space (defined in AP1 Lesson 4, where it is written x^
   R^{e\ast} | the projection of the constant 1 on the space of excess (zero-price) returns
   R_f | gross riskless return for the period, the reciprocal of the price of a sure payoff of 1
   \mathbb{Q} | a probability measure on the same space as \Prob, compared with it; by default an equivale
